Description: Fix surface_aggregator AggregateStatistics emplace for GCC 15
 GCC 15 libstdc++ std::optional::emplace() requires is_constructible_v<T>,
 which fails for aggregate types with default member initializers.
 .
 The AggregateStatistics struct has default member initializers (= false),
 making it an aggregate in C++20 that doesn't satisfy is_constructible_v.
 .
 Replace stats_.emplace() with assignment from aggregate initialization
 stats_ = AggregateStatistics{}.
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <vejeta@gmail.com>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/915400
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-12-03

diff --git a/components/viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.cc b/components/viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.cc
index d8c2a93..5ec0a7c 100644
--- a/components/viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.cc
+++ b/components/viz/service/display/surface_aggregator.cc
@@ -2161,7 +2161,10 @@ SurfaceAggregator::Aggregate(const SurfaceId& surface_id,
   root_surface_id_ = surface_id;

   // Start recording new stats for this aggregation.
-  stats_.emplace();
+  // GCC 15 libstdc++ std::optional::emplace() requires is_constructible_v,
+  // which fails for aggregates with default member initializers. Use
+  // assignment instead.
+  stats_ = AggregateStatistics{};

   ResolvedFrameData* resolved_frame = GetResolvedFrame(surface_id);

